## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant inference with strict data residency, budgets, and auditable lineage in a real-world GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation in Vertex AI Endpoints and Feature Store namespaces
- Routing logic with per-tenant budget and latency SLAs
- Data Catalog metadata tagging for lineage and governance
- Drift detection and rollback triggers per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function
async function routeRequest(tenantId, req) {
  const budgetOk = checkBudget(tenantId);
  const latencyOk = checkLatency(tenantId);
  const endpoint = budgetOk && latencyOk ? getTenantEndpoint(tenantId) : getSharedEndpoint();
  return await predict(endpoint, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in Feature Store and endpoints?
- How would you simulate rollback scenarios and validate audit trails?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end production-readiness: real-time latency, privacy across tenants, and governance with canary rollouts and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time inference with Vertex AI online endpoints and low-latency feature streaming
- Per-tenant feature stores for isolation; centralized ensemble for shared knowledge
- Privacy preservation via secure aggregation or differential privacy for cross-tenant signals
- Data provenance in BigQuery, Dataflow preprocessing, and strict cost controls with budgets
- Canary rollout, rollback criteria, and automated retraining cadence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: secure aggregation wrapper (conceptual)
function aggregateSecurely(tenantSignals) {
  // apply per-tenant masking, sum-aggregation, and reveal only aggregated result
  // actual DP/secure-aggregation libs would be used in prod
  const masked = tenantSignals.map(s => s + randomMask());
  return masked.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) - totalMask(masked.length);
}
```

